1
00:00:00,500 --> 00:00:07,500
Most finance apps make you type in every transaction.

2
00:00:08,000 --> 00:00:13,000
MoneyMind reads your bank statement directly.

3
00:00:13,200 --> 00:00:19,000
Gemini extracts every transaction. Categorizes them.

4
00:00:19,200 --> 00:00:25,000
Writes them to MongoDB Atlas — in real time.

5
00:00:25,500 --> 00:00:29,500
69 transactions. Six and a half seconds.

6
00:00:30,000 --> 00:00:36,000
And now the agent knows the user's actual life.

7
00:00:36,500 --> 00:00:41,500
Real spend. Real categories. From a real PDF.

8
00:00:42,000 --> 00:00:48,000
Most finance apps remember your transactions.

9
00:00:48,200 --> 00:00:54,000
MoneyMind remembers you. Your patterns, your context,

10
00:00:54,200 --> 00:01:01,500
the things you only said once. "I'm bulking this month."

11
00:01:02,000 --> 00:01:09,000
The next day, the next month, the next conversation —

12
00:01:09,200 --> 00:01:16,000
that context comes back. Vector recall over Voyage AI embeddings.

13
00:01:16,500 --> 00:01:23,000
When MoneyMind sees a pattern worth acting on,

14
00:01:23,200 --> 00:01:30,000
it proposes — and the user stays in control.

15
00:01:30,500 --> 00:01:37,000
Accept, decline, or modify. Here, modify to $250.

16
00:01:38,000 --> 00:01:44,000
The cap is alive. Saved to Atlas.

17
00:01:44,500 --> 00:01:51,500
The agent reads it back like it always knew.

18
00:01:52,500 --> 00:01:59,000
Built on Gemini and Vertex AI for reasoning.

19
00:01:59,200 --> 00:02:04,000
LangGraph orchestrates eighteen native agent tools.

20
00:02:04,200 --> 00:02:07,500
One MongoDB Atlas cluster.

21
00:02:08,000 --> 00:02:14,000
Eighteen tools across memory, goals, budgets, interventions.

22
00:02:14,200 --> 00:02:19,000
The agent decides when to use each one. The user just talks.

23
00:02:21,000 --> 00:02:27,000
MoneyMind. Remember the person, not just the transactions.
